-- allium: 3
-- The consumer boundary for a database served by the default or Multi driver.
-- Multi deployment registration uses an internal journal stream. Its writer reserves the name and incarnation before provisioning the data stream.
-- The writer orders readiness after observing the selected data stream and key authority. Nodes attach the ready incarnation and recover it on restart.
-- Flight administration requires a verified credential and an authority for the action and resources it names.
-- The installed administrative authorizer sees both resources for restore and fork.
-- Multi deletion first orders a terminal in the settled deployment stream. The catalog retains the incarnation, terminal, key generation and immutable retirement cutoff.
-- Key destruction and permanent journal deletion complete before the catalog records and authenticates erasure evidence.
-- A retirement with live dependent pins or unverified independent custody keys cannot close the deployment.
-- A private Multi custody transfer selects one source pin, source cut, destination incarnation and ordered reservation.
-- The source pin has no deadline and the destination stays private until its original authority confirms the installed backing and both copy drains.
-- A retry preserves the exact bound reservation through readiness and can recover the provider terminal after source pin release.
-- An inherited carrier read requires the mounted original authority and the destination's held generation through delivery.
-- A native custody fork selects the complete settled source cut and keeps original occurrence, placement and release identities under their source incarnation.
-- The source orders one forward enrollment for the exact copy and includes it in every contributing group's revocation inventory and drain.
-- The destination checkpoint retains the reciprocal enrollment and the source orders its drain after observing that readable backing.
-- Inherited native custody stays behind the original group authority and the original response admission.
-- A separately authenticated source observation can bind the pinned source cut, current writer epoch and current journal generation into the destination enrollment receipt.
-- The commissioned destination metadata selector returns the held generation, physical branch creation and exact native member winning a supplied valid instant at the restore and current cuts.
-- A private inherited point proof binds the exact destination restore and generation, physical branch creation, placement, selected application key and Original receipt.
-- Its release check observes the independently retained destination part and freshly verifies both attachments and the current Original writer fence.
-- A held carrier action reopens the exact copied event under the Original vault after observing the witnessed destination enrollment and independent application-family reader.
-- The opened projection holds the sealed carrier and link with all native contributor receipts from that point.
-- A separate transport credential admits the exact reserved part and nonce against the independent destination registration and the current Original writer.
-- Positive destination and Original terminal evidence disposes the same ordered registrations after revocation.

external entity ConsumerClient {
    -- A caller with credentials for the selected database.
}

external entity WireDatabase {
    -- The database incarnation selected when the call is admitted.
}

actor WireConsumer {
    identified_by: ConsumerClient
}

surface StatelessDatabase {
    facing consumer: WireConsumer
    context database: WireDatabase

    @guarantee CapabilityDiscovery
        -- A caller learns which operations and optional features the selected route can serve.
        -- An unavailable optional feature returns its name for comparison with Capabilities.
        -- A default attachment can serve guarded v1 writes over Classic effects covered by the shared main-branch fold.

    @guarantee ManagedWorkloadCreate
        -- A managed route accepts workload credentials from its configured issuer for its own audience.
        -- A workload credential binds one operation to an exact deployment name and incarnation for a bounded lifetime.
        -- Managed Create requires the explicit name and incarnation authorized by the credential.
        -- The catalog orders that identity before provisioning and the reply confirms the current matching attachment.
        -- A retry with a renewed grant can recover the same ordered identity.

    @guarantee IndependentManagedWorkloadIssuers
        -- A native Multi listener can enroll distinct HTTPS issuer origins, each with its own private roots, audience and reserved client ID prefix.
        -- Client credentials select exactly one issuer by disjoint prefix before token exchange.
        -- The Create issuer supplies a verified version 1 Create grant and the assignment issuer supplies a verified version 2 grant with one exact typed authority.
        -- Each issuer's verified subject and grant retain their receipt identity across the corresponding single-provider and combined profiles.
        -- The assignment issuer and configured Original authority point supply the ordered peer profile.

    @guarantee IndependentScopedAudienceIssuer
        -- The combined native Multi listener can enroll a third dedicated HTTPS origin and private roots for audience credentials.
        -- A reserved prefix selects this origin before token exchange and is disjoint from both workload prefixes.
        -- The audience issuer supplies an expiring label scope bound to the exact database name and incarnation with read labels and an empty write set.
        -- Audience calls use the verified scoped route and retain the same projected coordinates and receipt identity.
        -- Protected proof capture requires a separate positive grant in the label scope.
        -- Release and disposal use the separately authenticated Original custody authority.

    @guarantee ManagedWorkloadAssignment
        -- A bounded issuer grant authorizes one exact operation on the Original incarnation.
        -- The deployment owner configures the original main-branch authority point.
        -- Placement compares the applied predecessor version and requires positive original writer and close evidence for a retired holder.
        -- Claim compares the accepted fence version and orders its writer image and receipt together.
        -- Empty assignment closure races Claim on that same fence and publishes a positive vacant fence at the accepted higher epoch when it wins.
        -- The vacant fence preserves the last actual writer retirement and is usable as an exact successor predecessor.
        -- A guarded live close can require assignment-bound cold prerequisites in the same order as its server-authored closure.
        -- Write and close authenticate the exact fence and original claim receipt before either arm is considered.
        -- The current authority image must match at the configured valid time and at the writer's decision time.
        -- The original writer orders closure, placement replacement and mutation in the same stream.
        -- A cluster peer relays verified workload admission to the writer under the same configured issuer and authority point.
        -- The receiver checks the current incarnation and orders the unchanged namespace, attempt commitment and cutoff.
        -- An exact Root read captures at or before a cut confirmed by the active writer and rechecks the assignment before delivery.
        -- A tracked Root claim binds the original placement and writer and can guard writes in that exact assignment.
        -- A custody write grant commits the exact submitted action and admits only checked main-branch custody enrollment and data operations.
        -- A custody occurrence keeps its original applied receipt lineage under the workload namespace.
        -- A custody metadata reader names the live groups and observes only those groups and their placements at the selected original cut.
        -- Before a timed effect settles, the writer checks the original fence and the exclusive grant and request cutoffs again.
        -- A separate clear Root read grant names the same exact fence and writer receipt.
        -- Only the active local writer admits clear main Query and rechecks the authority at each frame handoff.
        -- Continuations retain the read grant namespace and may resume with its renewed credential.
        -- Named predecessor evidence returns only the authenticated fence, writer and close at their original applied cuts.
        -- The retained result binds the original namespace, key, operation family and immutable attempt commitment.
        -- An exact retry recovers the retained result independently of the former writer's current fence.
        -- Explicit receipt recovery can observe that outcome after closure, writer replacement, checkpoint and trim.
        -- Authorized settlement and a positive submit compete under the same durable attempt identity on the Original.
        -- A winning negative settlement refuses a later positive attempt under that identity.

    @guarantee CapturedRead
        -- Each successful query reports the basis of the database cut used for its rows.
        -- The database incarnation survives node restart and is shared by routes to the same database.
        -- A basis orders cuts within the selected database incarnation.
        -- The shared v1 encoding places the 16 incarnation bytes first, then the unsigned position as eight big-endian bytes.
        -- Applied-position drivers supply their applied position in this field.
        -- A branch query selects the requested branch and layer in the same fold that supplies transaction receipts.
        -- A Classic catalog query selects the installed replica cut as its basis.
        -- Exactly can reopen that Classic cut while it is the current published catalog.
        -- A local-layer read uses the branch's own writes at the selected cut.
        -- The temporal read driver supplies a system-time boundary as the basis position.
        -- Exactly selects its named cut.
        -- AtLeast returns a cut at or beyond its requested basis.
        -- AsOf applies a system-time ceiling to the selected cut.
        -- Where advertised, Linearizable establishes a fresh barrier within the call.

    @guarantee QueryContinuation
        -- A continuation reopens the same read basis and interpretation for the same ordered query and parameters.
        -- A successful final page has no continuation.
        -- Any authorized route to the same database incarnation can redeem a continuation while its cut and key generation are readable.
        -- A continuation binds its query, execution clock and next offset to the captured basis.
        -- Successive pages preserve the original token generation and share its retirement deadline.

    @guarantee RankedReads
        -- Text search returns matching rows ordered by descending relevance score.
        -- Vector nearest-neighbour reads return at most their requested limit ordered by ascending cosine distance.
        -- Ranking resolves rows at the query's selected cut.
        -- Bounded rank tables derive their totals from the effective candidate rows before paging.
        -- A tracked exact-cut rank with an empty window still returns its claim.
        -- RequireClearRankInput admits an unscoped tracked exact cut whose complete branch-view contributor inventory is proved empty.

    @guarantee RankedIvfQuery
        -- The negotiated ranked IVF query names one table, index and declaration generation at the tracked clear exact merged-main cut.
        -- A serving reader proves the generation against its retained primary catalogue and resolves the selected candidates at that same cut.
        -- Multi admits a writer-published catalogue for the exact incarnation, merged-main basis, clock and readable storage key generation.
        -- An assigned follower selects the catalogue in its applied prefix and retains it through delivery.
        -- Staged masks compare complete typed identities and filters constrain the effective candidate set before the zero-offset window.
        -- The trailer carries the executed generation, scored candidate count and approximation status with the basis and claim.
        -- A route advertises ranked IVF execution when its owner can capture and retain the paired physical catalogue.

    @guarantee QueryClaim
        -- A tracked query returns authenticated evidence naming its basis and an affected region that covers the query's dependencies.
        -- The same authority seals the claim and authenticates it when the writer evaluates Unchanged.
        -- The region can name rows, an index interval, a table, or the selected branch.
        -- The authority issues identical claim bytes for the same evidence under one key generation.

    @guarantee AssignedFollowerQuery
        -- The cell binds a private TLS listener to one exact local plain Multi replica under its deployment incarnation, placement epoch and assignment identity.
        -- A verified client presents the exact database and incarnation selector to use Capabilities and native Query on the assigned listener.
        -- The assigned residence follows the authenticated journal for the life of the listener.
        -- An installed follower node attaches the one prepared replica whose ready catalog registration matches the assignment.
        -- Its local copy follows the authenticated journal without entering writer election or recovery for the life of the process.
        -- Latest and AtLeast select the replica's locally applied head on merged main.
        -- Exactly selects a retained applied cut on merged main and echoes its opaque basis.
        -- A cut ahead of local apply, a missing retained cut and a different incarnation have distinct refusals.
        -- A progress reply binds the selected query basis and its recorded position to the assignment and the settled writer head from the authenticated committed prefix.
        -- The two positions share the incarnation's applied transaction coordinate.
        -- The cell drains admitted reads before stopping the assigned listener and retiring the assignment.
        -- The installed follower confirms detach for the exact slot, database, incarnation, placement epoch, assignment and bound endpoint after its listener, node and resource owners finish.

    @guarantee AssignedFollowerExactScope
        -- An open on the assigned follower retains the selected exact view under the authenticated Flight session for at most two seconds.
        -- The open attests the local basis, system time, applied position and assignment.
        -- A scoped read uses local apply evidence and is independent of writer progress.
        -- All scoped pages use the original view, basis and tracking mode.
        -- A scoped page with observation enabled attests the assignment and the selected applied position.
        -- Delivery requires the attached assignment and its captured key generation.
        -- A continuation identifies its exact scope and the request that issued it.
        -- Closing or expiring the scope ends admission and cancels its active pages.

    @guarantee ReceiverClockObservation
        -- Where advertised, the first page includes a sample from the installed receiver clock when requested.
        -- The authenticated observation binds the sample, selected cut, query fingerprint and Flight session.
        -- The query trailer reports the selected system time separately.

    @guarantee DeclaredTableSchema
        -- A table is open until it declares a schema, and declared from then until it is dropped.
        -- An open table admits any column a write carries.
        -- A schema declaration names a non-null _id field of type Utf8, keyword, Int64 or UUID.
        -- It declares no temporal column: RTDB maintains _valid_from, _valid_to, _system_from and _system_to on every row.
        -- A redeclaration keeps the _id type and each declared column's type, and may add columns; omitted columns stay declared.
        -- A table's first declaration admits every row version the table already holds.
        -- A query of a declared table resolves _id, the declared columns and the temporal columns before any row is written.
        -- A declared table refuses a write, through Transact or a Classic source, that carries an undeclared column, a value of another type than its declared column, or an ID of another type than its _id.
        -- A null value conforms to any declared column.
        -- Checkpoints and followers retain whether a table is declared, its _id type and its declared columns.

    @guarantee StandaloneStoreContract
        -- A standalone installation's Flight listener serves rtdb.store.v1 and rtdb.admin.v1 of the v1 surface, and nothing else of it.
        -- It refuses every other rtdb.v1 action and every rtdb.v1 query or changes ticket.

    @guarantee OrderedIndexCatalog
        -- An ordered index declaration preserves its columns in the order sent by the caller.
        -- Query of xt.ordered_indexes reads the definitions present at its selected applied cut.
        -- A binary or text range guard can name a single-column index, and an unbounded count can name a compound index.

    @guarantee RankedIndexCatalog
        -- A ranked declaration binds its index name, ordered columns, and kind-specific options at the applied transaction position.
        -- Query of xt.ranked_indexes reads the definitions present at its selected cut and their serving mode and artefact readiness.
        -- Search declarations also supply analyzer and history definitions to the search accelerator.
        -- A declaration on an exact-SQL route reports artefacts_ready false for a physical index that the route cannot prove.
        -- VerifyRankedArtefacts checks the storage placement paired with the selected clear exact cut.
        -- Spatial readiness requires a persisted posting file for every selected primary trie in the same placement and declared generation.
        -- Where a provider version is recorded, the response supplying the persisted file names that exact version.
        -- The serving mode and approximate status describe the permitted query path.

    @guarantee CountConstraintCatalog
        -- A count range limits one ordered index interval.
        -- A grouped count limits every qualifying binary key or key prefix at the constraint's valid time.
        -- Binary predicates select qualifying rows by equality on the named columns.
        -- The writer checks the final state of the selected arm before committing its effects.
        -- An unrestricted Query reads the installed typed definitions in xt.count_constraints at its selected cut.

    @guarantee TransactionRelativeValidTime
        -- Put and Delete on unlabelled tables may name a valid-time endpoint as a signed offset from the transaction time.
        -- The writer resolves both endpoints against the receipt's system time and records the resolved interval.
        -- Overflow, a reversed interval and an empty interval fail before any row effect is applied.

    @guarantee WrittenBasis
        -- Where advertised, a caller can explicitly select _rtdb_written_basis for a visible row version.
        -- It names the row version rather than the selected query cut and can be supplied to a Version guard.
        -- A Classic written basis keeps the transaction identity preserved by the resolved record or the retained event position.
        -- An imported legacy row without transaction provenance returns a null written basis.
        -- For a scoped query, the returned basis uses the reader's projection domain.

    @guarantee TokenAuthority
        -- All routes to an incarnation use the same wrapped token key for each published generation.
        -- New queries use the latest published generation.
        -- An earlier generation remains usable until its retirement deadline while the selected view is readable.
        -- Redeeming a token whose generation is erased returns erased-under-view.

    @guarantee TransactionReceipt
        -- A route that advertises writes returns its selected outcome with the applied basis and system time.
        -- A matching committed request returns the stored receipt for its key.
        -- The idempotency key within its receipt namespace identifies the request.
        -- The writer records its admission time, the complete canonical request and the selected outcome with resolved effects.
        -- Followers apply the recorded effects. Checkpoints preserve the namespaced key, request digest and outcome for retries.
        -- A Classic migration can import authenticated canonical receipts whose original installed coordinates map to retained native cuts.
        -- The imported canonical receipt keeps its namespace, key, request digest and outcome.
        -- Classic-only receipt controls preserve the original lookup identity through authenticated read-through.
        -- Validation evaluates requirements and guards at a fresh basis and leaves the applied position unchanged.

    @guarantee FundedDecisionClock
        -- A writer advertises transact.decision-clock-offer after installing an authenticated receiver clock, a certificate verifier and a journal provider that attests the timed original quorum.
        -- The receiver supplies a live observation from the installed durable clock domain when the writer checks certificate expiry for advertisement.
        -- The stock receiver verifies a bounded private challenge response over the purpose, source, domain, exact certificate digest and signed evidence digest.
        -- The receiver authority durably orders the positive publisher epoch and sequence across replacements and signs the fresh sample within the certified clock bounds.
        -- The installed issuer signs the exact attachment, service scope, expiry and clock margins.
        -- The admitted predecessor belongs to that attachment even when its coordinate is projected on the wire.
        -- A funded request lists transact.decision-clock-offer among its required capabilities.
        -- OfferDecisionClock books the exact canonical Transact request and predecessor under the caller's existing receipt key and namespace.
        -- A retry of that booking recovers the original seat.
        -- Transact field 8 consumes the seat under the same request, caller and incarnation.
        -- The original receiver lineage and the inclusive lower and exclusive upper bounds govern eligibility.
        -- A fresh acceptance uses the booked certificate under the current receiver authority.
        -- The advertised reading supplies transaction-relative terms.
        -- The original-quorum append binds the receiver certificate and exclusive journal cutoff to the exact accepting record.
        -- Receipt field 9 preserves the original offer on terminal acknowledgement and keyed recovery.
        -- A scoped request evaluates an effect-free validation against its projected history and returns only the opaque booking and projected predecessor.
        -- Independently identical receiver evidence and projected histories produce identical scoped outcomes.

    @guarantee FundedAppointment
        -- An authenticated Original writer sees transact.funded-appointment on a route with an installed receiver and positive timed original journal capacity.
        -- PrepareFundedAppointment reserves the native key and one absent main-branch receipt point, identified by its table, typed ID and explicit valid time.
        -- Preparation binds the Original predecessor and business intent digest to an inert booking, the advertised reading and separate exclusive receiver and journal cutoffs.
        -- ActivateFundedAppointment uses the same key and booking and orders the guarded control writes together before the advertised reading.
        -- Activation requires at least two explicitly guarded control points and absence of the exact business receipt.
        -- Final Transact field 9 supplies the booking and intent digest and requires transact.funded-appointment.
        -- The final request requires the original activation Basis on two distinct live control points, the exact business receipt's absence and the caller's live prerequisites.
        -- Live requirements use the authenticated decision observation, and transaction-relative terms use the advertised reading.
        -- The selected terminal arm creates the exact business receipt point alongside its effects and settlement.
        -- Activation and the accepting terminal each verify the original timed append proof for their exact sealed record under the retained certificate.
        -- Each stage accepts an exact retry by canonical request, and one canonical final request can consume the active appointment.
        -- Prepare returns the preparation Basis, and Activate and terminal Receipt field 10 return the original activation Basis and bounds.
        -- Keyed status is pending until a terminal publishes and then returns the original terminal Basis, system time and appointment after the window closes.
        -- An ordered exclusion at the same Original receipt point blocks later consumption while leaving the appointment's keyed status pending.
        -- A commissioned managed call uses the same actions and wire fields under an independently authenticated v2 funded-appointment grant.
        -- The grant binds the exact database and incarnation, current placement and namespaced ClaimWriter, one native key, one typed receipt point, the business intent and its approved funding context.
        -- The managed call can prepare, activate, consume and recover only that appointment in its private receipt namespace.
        -- The managed appointment route admits clear Original history and clear effects under the managed workload custody checks.
        -- The managed writer validates any tracked read claims against the same placement and ClaimWriter binding.
        -- Managed status returns pending before the terminal publishes and returns the exact terminal with field 10 under a current grant for the same scope.

    @guarantee TransactionRequirements
        -- A write route that supports requirements advertises transact.requires.
        -- TransactRequest carries the ordered requires list as repeated Guard at protobuf field 7.
        -- Each requirement is a precondition on the original state.
        -- Passing all requirements allows guards to select an arm.
        -- The first failed requirement selects a Refused receipt with category conflict and code rtdb/requirement-failed.
        -- The refusal carries only the zero-based requirement index in its message and applies no row or catalog effects.
        -- A request with operations in either arm records that receipt for replay and TxStatus.
        -- A scoped receipt carries the basis and system time of the admitted projection.

    @guarantee PhysicalErasure
        -- A route that supports physical erasure advertises erasure.
        -- An applied erase removes row values from the clean checkpoint and orders retirement of the preceding journal and checkpoint generation.
        -- Default requires evidence for the source prefix, replica prefix and every prior recovery dependency.
        -- An enrolled Kafka route requires the original writable Local residence, both original sealed topics and a recoverable suffix.
        -- The writer verifies the retained offset and replica reference evidence before a new Kafka erase decision.
        -- The clean native recovery cut binds the applied source position, its replica boundary and the exact uploaded block digest.
        -- The selected native checkpoint authenticates under the successor generation and retains the pending receipt at the erased basis.
        -- The Default writer holds later source decisions while it rewrites the physical main fold at that cut.
        -- The sealed shared image binds the rewritten table blocks and trie bodies to the exact recovery boundary.
        -- A term-admitted upload fixes the selected checkpoint before the writer records the original retirement deadline.
        -- A replacement recovers that deadline from the replica suffix before continuing retirement.
        -- The receipt carries the original unreadable-by deadline after provider-specific completion.
        -- A pending Default erasure receipt stays private to the fold until the ordered terminal verifies reader drain, log and object closure and predecessor key destruction.
        -- Replayed erase receipts preserve that deadline after trim.
        -- Previously opened query and change streams verify their selected generation at each frame handoff.
        -- A Default view reopened from a sealed checkpoint keeps the authenticated generation of that image through frame delivery.

    @guarantee ProtectedPlacement
        -- A route that serves row custody orders original placement, reservation, activation and revocation in the same database fold.
        -- A reservation binds the exact original and reviewed source occurrences to fresh destination and link identities, a target validity rule and the reviewed carrier and link bytes.
        -- A derived write can reserve and activate its destination together after the original occurrence orders earlier in the same transaction arm.
        -- A separately reserved placement activates at a later basis and resolves relative target validity at the accepting placement clock.
        -- Only the ordered write at the reserved target can activate the destination, and its basis, within-transaction ordinal and encrypted envelope become part of the occurrence commitment.
        -- A same-database branch inherits the original occurrence through its fork basis.
        -- The inventory includes inactive reservations and active occurrences, so a new reservation or activation invalidates an earlier revocation plan.
        -- Revocation permanently closes placement and release admission.
        -- An exact retry can recover the original receipt even after its custody key has been destroyed.
        -- A tracked exact merged Query by the original writer can authenticate a reviewed non-main source point and the complete native group inventory at that cut.
        -- The same Query seals the reviewed branch, cut, validity point, Original and winning physical occurrence into its release proof and independently confirms both writing receipts.
        -- The reviewed reservation records its transaction key and basis and commits the source evidence alongside the destination and link identities.
        -- The accepting arm checks the retained reservation receipt and the current writer, source and group inventory, then places the protected main rows and drops the reviewed branch together.
        -- Exact placement and branch catalogue readback at the accepted basis pairs the retained activation with its keyed transaction receipt after branch drop.
        -- An installed Original bridge distinguishes the canonical landing request commitment from the acceptance body commitment bound after sealing.
        -- Original activation requires the exact native reservation and accepted receipts and both body witnesses written at the accepting basis.
        -- The native fold recovers the opaque carrier and link from the accepted placement after the source branch drops.
        -- The installed native Original family vault retains authored stage enrollment before sealing and confirms membership using the exact keyed write and native occurrence.
        -- A named authoring branch binds its supplied line UUID to the exact writable branch creation and line registration co-ordered by the current mounted Original writer.
        -- The vault retains that line identity across the family's authored occurrences and rejects its reuse on a different branch creation.
        -- A rewrite binds the enrolled live source and the linked native reservation to the new authored occurrence.
        -- The generic Original action opens only an activated or confirmed stage under an exactly promoted release registration and retains a family hold through the positive disposition.
        -- A family close binds the exact applied native group revocation to the independent family stage inventory.
        -- Family stage destruction requires both the native release and copy drain and the disposal of every Original family hold.
        -- Revocation masks the matching occurrences through all retained ancestor views and drains their existing release holds before native key destruction.
        -- Scoped readers receive custody evidence as an opaque read handle.

    @guarantee ProtectedResponseRelease
        -- The installed original carrier journal authenticates the exact attachment, original writer, response part, admitted occurrence and immutable cutoff.
        -- The original writer and carrier receipt are observed independently and verified by exact request key, basis and system time on the original attachment.
        -- Default verifies receipt installation in the canonical v1 fold and validates the exact generation held by the protected view.
        -- The carrier receipt selects the admitted occurrence and its commitment is retained in the release registration.
        -- The response release command checks the observed writer version in the same order as the hold or terminal.
        -- The writer version must own both its configured valid-time point and the current valid-time point at the ordered decision.
        -- An authenticated host mount pins the original writer and provider to the live writable database attachment.
        -- The cross-process provider response authenticates its exact challenge, operation, authority and payload with the configured registry signing key.
        -- The configured original owner may request a sealed read proof bound to its authenticated session, attachment mount, selected basis and key generation.
        -- The same unscoped Original owner Query reports each contributor's physical authoring branch, ordinal and exact retained placement receipt, including inherited contributors and dependencies absent from the result.
        -- The contributor inventory requires an unambiguous enrolled write and a retained applied receipt at its written basis and clock.
        -- A private release preflight binds the exact proof list, full contributor inventory and frame commitment to the independently observed original response part.
        -- Removing the mount or detaching its database closes new handoffs and preserves already ordered release evidence.
        -- The response owner holds every group and occurrence in its authenticated contributor inventory through delivery.
        -- A native ranked capture retains protected inputs before ranking or slicing, including inherited and shadowing versions.
        -- Before enqueue the mounted owner rechecks the exact frame commitment, complete promoted inventory, attachment, selected key generation and immutable deadline.
        -- The ordered release fold serializes private registration, promotion, whole-part admission, cancellation and disposal with revocation.
        -- Whole-part admission binds one frame and the complete promoted contributor inventory under an immutable cutoff and requires every contributor's group to be live.
        -- A transport may enqueue once through the original pending reservation using its fresh admission and unexpired cutoff.
        -- A retained admission replay is available to recovery and grants no enqueue authority.
        -- Every admitted part stays in each contributing group's drain until the exact original carrier terminal, including across loss of a reply or process restart.
        -- Only private cancellation or authenticated durable transport disposal terminates an admitted release.
        -- Recovery retains the original terminal decision and evidence through checkpoint and trim.
        -- A revoked group's release holds drain before key destruction.
        -- A route advertises row custody once its protected readers, release adapters and key enforcement support these guarantees.
        -- An installed Multi writer uses durable group-key retirement and shares its row-custody feature set with the single and batched resolvers.
        -- The reviewed placement capability in either mode requires the configured Original owner's live provider mount and current writer receipt.

    @guarantee ChangesCoverage
        -- Changes reports its covered interval even when there are no changes for the selected tables.
        -- An applied-position route takes its coverage from the driver's retained effect history.
        -- After opening a default branch checkpoint, the retained change interval starts at the checkpoint's basis.
        -- A reported erasure has a key when keys are requested and omits both row images.
        -- Default and Multi report the previous image at a closure and the new image at an opening.
        -- A returned page carries whole system-time groups.
        -- An expired starting cut returns the cursor-expired code.
        -- A waiting call returns after a relevant change, complete coverage of its requested interval or expiry of its wait.

    @guarantee ChangesProgress
        -- Where advertised, progress-only Changes returns the schema and coverage trailer for the request.
        -- The same table admission, group limits, wait and coverage rules apply to a progress-only request.

    @guarantee ScopedVisibilityCapability
        -- Scoped visibility is a target capability specified by ScopedRowVisibility in allium/rtdb-multi.allium.
        -- A route without an applied scoped projection omits row-visibility from Capabilities.
        -- An OIDC label scope binds its credential to the verified database name and incarnation.
        -- A scoped credential requires a route that enforces that scope for every admitted operation.
        -- The initial scoped serving path selects merged main and uses a logical system-time coordinate.
        -- Default mode and Multi use the same scoped projection for Query, Changes, and transaction receipts.
        -- Changes waits for progress observable by the selected scope or the requested deadline.
        -- Put rows can supply literal signed-microsecond valid-time bounds in _valid_from and _valid_to.

    @guarantee ScopedExactHold
        -- A route advertising row-visibility.exact-hold accepts the authenticated ScopedHold action.
        -- Retain positively orders a quota-accounted lease for the projected cut and its clear publication version at the supplied valid instant.
        -- Query scoped_hold selects the same projected Exactly cut and fixed valid instant on every page.
        -- Reopen authenticates the issuing scope and checks the exclusive deadline and live retained publication.
        -- The retain and release transitions persist in both native transaction folds.

    @guarantee ScopedCustodyEvidence
        -- A protected scoped route advertising row-visibility.custody-release accepts custody_release_evidence on Query and Changes.
        -- The trailer includes a single opaque proof handle for the captured contributor set, including a complete empty set.
        -- The checked Original action confirms the private native occurrence receipts and exact registered frame.
        -- A successful scoped admission response returns only the application response state.
        -- Positive Original disposal settles promoted registrations independently of the read-proof lifetime.

    @guarantee ManagedOriginalCustodyControl
        -- An assignment issuer can authenticate a release or disposal credential scoped to the exact installed database, configured Original owner and provider authority.
        -- Release resolves scoped proof handles and checks or admits the exact registered response part.
        -- The registered frame fixes the complete native contributor inventory and cutoff before the writer prepares its ordered holds.
        -- The cutoff fits within the lease of the release credential and each selected proof.
        -- A separate disposal credential confirms positive transport disposition and the exact revoked group drain.
        -- Original writer identity and delivery fences remain current when the writer admits the response.

    @guarantee ManagedOriginalFamilyPlacement
        -- An independently commissioned issuer and placement signer authorize one Original owner, database incarnation, named writable branch creation, custody family, group and assignment epoch.
        -- The active local writer verifies the mounted Original's signed writer observation against the exact ordered assignment and writer receipts.
        -- The family credential serves capabilities, the private family action and an exact tracked merged Query selecting a confirmed occurrence.
        -- The Query exposes the selected point identity and binds its claim, reviewed evidence and delivery to that session, mount and credential lifetime.
        -- The claim authenticates the exact unpaged tracked reviewed row Query, its receipt namespace and session, the current writer and the immutable creation Basis of the granted branch.
        -- The family action enrolls and seals stages before it accepts a signed exact placement request for those stages.
        -- The retained authoring reserve resolves the founding and winning author frames inside the Original vault at their exact namespaced Then receipts.
        -- The vault verifies the named line generation, physical carrier point, full reviewed contributors, carrier digests and current delivery authority before acknowledging the retained reservation.
        -- The retained reservation binds the opaque proof and Claim to the subsequent signed order.
        -- A reviewed reservation consumes the claim and proof from the same Query.
        -- The accepting arm settles the retained namespaced reservation, protected placement, paired application witnesses and source drop together under the current assignment and deadline.
        -- Family receipt recovery derives the position from the enrolled placement and reads the credential's retained namespace at that position.
        -- A family on an imported attachment starts after its current ClaimWriter and retains only receipts strictly after the import fence.
        -- Branch creation is confirmed at the registered creation Basis and authoring is confirmed at the physical occurrence's Written Basis.
        -- The active epoch can recover its exact landing after the source branch drops.

    @guarantee ManagedOriginalBranchProvisioning
        -- An independent provision grant commits the exact request, current Original writer, configured registry, named line generation and application owner point.
        -- One accepting arm forks the retained clear main Basis and co-writes the owner point and one main registry row at the branch creation Basis.
        -- At valid time zero the registry row identifies the child by name, generation, creation Basis, raw creation key and owner.
        -- Receipt readback uses the provision namespace and operation family at a Basis strictly after the import fence when present.

    @guarantee ManagedOriginalFamilyReadback
        -- A separate issuer commissions a readback bearer for the current Original installation, attachment, assignment fence, ClaimWriter, named creation, family and group.
        -- The Original mount commissions seven distinct application relations for carrier, member, admission, business receipt, execution, publication and Root version evidence.
        -- The bearer selects exact lineage and registry observations and a literal point on the mounted carrier relation at its commissioned Basis.
        -- The lineage observation attests the authenticated parent Basis and system time from the retained cut coordinate.
        -- A written carrier selection returns its point coordinates and authenticated absence requires a readable exact view.
        -- One commissioned native receipt binds the placement catalog and its exact co-written application witnesses.
        -- The reader returns only the commissioned member mapping after the source drops, and main landing settlement uses the exact accepted cut.
        -- Execution settlement returns commitments to the cells written under the keyed author receipt.
        -- The reader confirms current writer, attachment, family and grant through response delivery.

    @guarantee ChangesImages
        -- Changes image columns carry individual Arrow IPC streams by default.
        -- A route advertising changes.images.stream-v1 accepts an explicit request for shared image streams and acknowledges the selected representation in the response.
        -- In the shared representation each present image column carries one Arrow IPC stream in its first cell, with one image per result row in that batch's order.
        -- Image selection, change ordering and covered intervals apply equally to both representations.
}
